    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d257">

                <pb facs="0345" n="331" sameAs="frus:frus1948v05p1/pg331"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">501.BC/4–1048</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum of Conversation, by the Director of the
                        Office of Near Eastern and African Affairs</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Henderson</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1948-04-10">April 10, 1948</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>During the course of a conversation I had with the Afghan Minister<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d257-f1"/> this afternoon, he handed me the attached document, which
                    he said was a copy of a document which he had given to the British Delegation to
                    the Security Council during the course of the discussions with regard to the
                    future of Kashmir. The Minister said that he had given this paper to the British
                    Delegation in order that it would be clearly understood that Afghanistan
                    considers itself to have a vital interest in the future of the tribal areas.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>L. W. H[<hi rendition="#small-caps">enderson</hi>]</signed>
                </closer>


                <xi:include href="d257-a1.xml" xpointer="d257-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d257-f1" n="1" xml:id="d257-f1-content">
                <p>Abdol Hosayn Aziz.</p>
            </note>
